  "details": "Object sync'ed Objects that start off in the world always have an owner assigned. This means that someone in the world is always able to execute a trigger with the owner broadcast type. When the owner of the object leaves the room, the master is assigned as the new owner, allowing them to execute owner broadcasts on this object. This ownership transfer does not fire the OnOwnershipTransfer event. With this setup, there is no way to know if the object's owner left the room and handle it.\n\nAs for spawned object sync'ed objects, when the owner of the object leaves the room, the owner is set to null. This means no one in the room is able to execute a trigger with the owner broadcast type. The OnOwnershipTransfer event again is not fired. Since owner triggers will not execute, it is possible to detect if a the owner left by combining OnPlayerLeft with the owner broadcast type and seeing if it ever executes. \n\nPlease change the behavior of synced world objects to be like spawned objects in that the owner is set to null.\n\nRelated canny posts:\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/onownershiptransfer-triger-fires-when-any-ownership-transfer-happend\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/object-sync-objects-have-no-assigned-owner-when-original-owner-leaves-instance",
